  "lyrics": "Intro]\nYeah\nZip that up\nWe outside\n\n[Verse 1]\nClock on my hoodie, time on my back\nStill runnin' late but I\u2019m right on track\nMama said \u201cPray,\u201d homie said \u201cTrap\u201d\nI just hit the pad, turn story to rap\nBus stop breeze in the cold of December\nHands in my sleeves, tryna warm this temper\nLandlord callin', I mute that number\nGot dreams too big for a small-ass summer\nNoodles on the stove, steam in the kitchen\nPhone on the floor with a cracked-up vision\nScrolling through lives that look so different\nThen I see the mirror, it\u2019s me that\u2019s missin'\n\n[Chorus]\nI came up broke, but I don\u2019t stay stuck\nTurned every setback into straight luck\nThey wrote me off, I just wrote more\nPut my whole heart in a 16 bar\nI came up small in a big man\u2019s town\nTalked to the sky till the sky talked down\nNow when they ask what I pray for now\nI just say \u201cPeace\u201d and I still get loud (yeah)\n\n[Verse 2]\nShort fuse, big heart, that\u2019s a bad mix\nGrew up learnin\u2019 all the wrong magic tricks\nMake pain disappear, hide that quick\nSmile in the pic, storm in the attic\nCouch made a home for a couple of months\nFriends turned ghosts when the vibes got rough\nStill send love when the text get tough\n\u2018Cause hate on my name ain\u2019t payin\u2019 me much\nLil sis watchin', I can\u2019t just fold\nShe deserve more than my \u201cmaybe\u201d goals\nSo I lace shoes, take that road\nFeet get sore but the soul stay bold (yeah)\n\n[Chorus]\nI came up broke, but I don\u2019t stay stuck\nTurned every setback into straight luck\nThey wrote me off, I just wrote more\nPut my whole heart in a 16 bar\nI came up small in a big man\u2019s town\nTalked to the sky till the sky talked down\nNow when they ask what I pray for now\nI just say \u201cPeace\u201d and I still get loud (still get loud)\n\n[Bridge]\nHands up high for the days we feared\nHands down low for the weight we shared\nEyes to the ground but the mind so clear\nIf you feel that, sing it right here (right here)\n\n[Chorus]\nI came up broke, but I don\u2019t stay stuck\nTurned every setback into straight luck\nThey wrote me off, I just wrote more\nPut my whole heart in a 16 bar\nI came up small in a big man\u2019s town\nTalked to the sky till the sky talked down\nNow when they ask what I pray for now\nI just say \u201cPeace\u201d and I still get loud (get loud)",
  "title": "Clock On My Hoodie",
