  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe morning breaks on a whiteboard slate\nSmall scratches left by a heavy hand\nA trial run for a digital fate\nTracing lines through the shifting sand\nThe cursor blinks in a rhythmic beat\nWatching the ink go cold and dry\nNotes scattered down a one-way street\nUnder the glare of a paper sky\n\n[Verse]\nIt is a simple script in a complex frame\nChecking the gears of the grand machine\nCalling a ghost by a secret name\nHidden away in the logic screen\nTesting the pulse of the wire and bone\nHearing the hum of the silver core\nStanding inside of the vast unknown\nKnocking once on an open door\n\n[Chorus]\nThis is the fresh foundation stone\nSetting the pace for the miles to come\nBuilding a world that is all our own\nOut of the silence and the strum\nTesting the strength of the new design\nFinding the truth in the darkest blue\nCrossing the edge of the border line\nMaking the old world something new\n\n[Bridge]\nThe static clears from the dusty air\nThe signal grows with a steady light\nA sudden spark in a quiet glare\nCutting a path through the longest night\nNothing is lost if it starts today\nNothing is broken that cannot mend\nWalking along the iron way\nReady to reach for the furthest end\n\n[Verse]\nLeave the mistakes on the cutting floor\nPick up the pieces and start again\nNobody knows what the marks are for\nWriting it out with a steady pen\nA casual phrase in a brand new tongue\nCarving a shape in the hollow space\nSongs that remain to be loudly sung\nFinding a home in a foreign place\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe first breath taken in the dawn\nThe long road stretching to the sea\nEvery shadow is finally gone\nSetting the heavy spirit free\n\n[Chorus]\nThis is the fresh foundation stone\nSetting the pace for the miles to come\nBuilding a world that is all our own\nOut of the silence and the strum\nTesting the strength of the new design\nFinding the truth in the darkest blue\nCrossing the edge of the border line\nMaking the old world something