  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe dust settles hard on the gravel track\nA sudden wind begins to howl and pull back\nStray thoughts like crows on a wire fence\nCounting the miles in the past tense\nI found a copper coin half buried in the clay\nWhere the red sun bleeds the blue away\nThe highway lines are blurred and faded thin\nWaiting for the first movement to begin\n\n[Verse]\nOld shoes scuffing up the yellow grain\nThinking about the pattern of the rain\nThere is a silence that keeps no time\nA mountain peak no one cares to climb\nI saw a shadow stretching tall and lean\nAcross a valley that the world has never seen\nNo maps were folded no compass cast\nJust a long reflection of the very last\n\n[Chorus]\nThe first song is a rattle in the throat\nA simple melody kept afloat\nBefore the symphony finds its heavy hand\nIt is a single footprint in the sand\nThe tuning of a heart on a hollow floor\nOpening up a wide and unlatched door\nStriking the match and watching the wick\nHearing the gears of the seasons click\n\n[Verse]\nA tattered coat hanging from a crooked limb\nThe light around the edges growing dim\nWords are just pebbles in a silver stream\nWashed away before they form a dream\nI met a man who spoke in ancient sighs\nWith a thousand different winters in his eyes\nHe said the beginning is a heavy weight\nBetter to be early than to be late\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe air is holding its collective breath\nBetween the living and the phantom death\nClear the throat and let the spirit fly\nUnder the heavy dome of a copper sky\n\n[Chorus]\nThe first song is a rattle in the throat\nA simple melody kept afloat\nBefore the symphony finds its heavy hand\nIt is a single footprint in the sand\nThe tuning of a heart on a hollow floor\nOpening up a wide and unlatched door\nStriking the match and watching the wick\nHearing the gears of the seasons click\n\n[Chorus]\nThe first song is a rattle in the throat\nA simple melody kept afloat\nBefore the symphony finds its heavy hand\nIt is a single footprint in the sand\nThe tuning of a heart on a hollow floor\nOpening up a wide and unlatched door\nStriking the match and watching the wick\nHearing the gears of the seasons click",
