  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe first act was a stumble through the dark\nA wooden match sticking to a dying spark\nI spent my silver on a story already told\nWatching the copper turn back into cold\nNow the dust has settled on the spinning plate\nI\u2019m standing early at the garden gate\n\n[Chorus]\nGive me the second song the one that knows the way\nThe melody that didn't have a single word to say\nBeyond the first impression and the hollow pride\nWhere the river meets the salt of the rising tide\nIt\u2019s the grace of the encore when the lights are low\nThe only truth I ever really needed to know\n\n[Verse]\nA ghost is dancing in the upper room\nSweeping out the shadows with a tattered broom\nI left my ego by the side of the road\nUnderneath the weight of a heavy load\nDon't tell me about the glory of the start\nI\u2019m looking for the rhythm of a steady heart\n\n[Chorus]\nGive me the second song the one that knows the way\nThe melody that didn't have a single word to say\nBeyond the first impression and the hollow pride\nWhere the river meets the salt of the rising tide\nIt\u2019s the grace of the encore when the lights are low\nThe only truth I ever really needed to know\n\n[Bridge]\nThe clock is ticking but the gears are loose\nI\u2019m finally cutting through the golden noose\nYou can keep the fanfare and the grand design\nI\u2019ll take the water that turned into wine\n\n[Chorus]\nGive me the second song the one that knows the way\nThe melody that didn't have a single word to say\nBeyond the first impression and the hollow pride\nWhere the river meets the salt of the rising tide\nIt\u2019s the grace of the encore when the lights are low\nThe only truth I ever really needed to know\n\n[Chorus]\nGive me the second song the one that knows the way\nThe melody that didn't have a single word to say\nBeyond the first impression and the hollow pride\nWhere the river meets the salt of the rising tide\nIt\u2019s the grace of the encore when the lights are low\nThe only truth I ever really needed to know",
