  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe blank page is a cold stretch of white sand\nWaiting for the weight of a heavy hand\nThe ink is a river that refuses to flow\nLooking for a place where the wild seeds grow\nI picked up a stone from the edge of the town\nWhere the old iron fences are all falling down\nThere is no map for the road I must take\nJust a shivering light on a dark timber lake\n\n[Verse]\nThe clock on the wall has a hollow metallic sound\nCounting the footsteps of ghosts on the ground\nI\u2019m carving a name into the bark of a tree\nTrying to remember what used to be free\nThe shadows are long and the shadows are deep\nLike secrets a mountain is trying to keep\nThe first line is written in dust and in bone\nA message sent out to the vast and unknown\n\n[Chorus]\nIt is a long way from the start to the end\nAround every corner and every sharp bend\nThe wind is a prophet with nothing to say\nBut blow all the ashes of yesterday away\nYes the sky is a mirror of silver and lead\nReflecting the visions inside of my head\n\n[Chorus]\nIt is a long way from the start to the end\nAround every corner and every sharp bend\nThe wind is a prophet with nothing to say\nBut blow all the ashes of yesterday away\nYes the sky is a mirror of silver and lead\nReflecting the visions inside of my head\n\n[Bridge]\nThey told me the truth was a jewel in a box\nSafe from the hammers and hidden by locks\nBut I found the key in a bucket of rain\nTied to the wheels of a slow moving train\nThe morning is coming but the night is still near\nWhispering things that I don't want to hear\nSo I buckle my boots and I sharpen my sight\nWalking straight into the belly of light\n\n[Verse]\nThe melody crawls like a vine up the wall\nCatching the leaves just before they can fall\nI\u2019ve seen the poets who stood in the queue\nTrading their stories for something brand new\nBut I\u2019ll keep my tattered and weathered old coat\nAnd the jagged red lines of the verses I wrote\nThe beginning is always a gamble with time\nSearching for reason and searching for rhyme\n\n[Verse]\nThe wheels of the wagon are beginning to creak\nWhile the strong men are silent and the loud men are weak\nI\u2019m casting a net in a dry dusty well\nHoping to find what the stars have to tell\nThe first song is sung by a bird on a wire\nWho isn't afraid of the frost or the fire\nAnd when the last note has faded from view\nThe world will be open and shining and blue\n\n[Chorus]\nIt is a long way from the start to the end\nAround every corner and every sharp bend\nThe wind is a prophet with nothing to say\nBut blow all the ashes of yesterday away\nYes the sky is a mirror of silver and lead\nReflecting the visions inside of my head\n\n[Chorus]\nIt is a long way from the start to the end\nAround every corner and every sharp bend\nThe wind is a prophet with nothing to say\nBut blow all the ashes of yesterday away\nYes the sky is a mirror of silver and lead\nReflecting the visions inside of my head",
