  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe needle drops on a circle of black stone\nThe dust begins to dance in a light of its own\nYou turned the page before the ink was dry\nUnderneath a charcoal smudge of an endless sky\nThe highway is hummed by a ghost in the tires\nMoving past the skeletons of telephone wires\n\n[Verse]\nA suitcase sits heavy with the things you forgot\nThe maps are all folded in a tight heavy knot\nThe sunrise is bleeding through a crack in the door\nTelling you the old ways don't work anymore\nIt\u2019s a long slow climb up the side of the hill\nWhere the air is heavy and the clocks stand still\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe shadows are stretching like fingers of fate\nTracing the lines on an iron gate\nThe silence is louder than the thunder could be\nAnd the wind is a river flowing out to the sea\n\n[Chorus]\nPlay it again for the hearts in the dark\nLeaving behind every smoldering spark\nTurning the corner where the pavement ends\nTracing the shape where the horizon bends\nSing it out loud for the miles left to go\nThe only direction that the weary can know\n\n[Verse]\nThe prophets are sleeping on the benches of wood\nMisunderstanding what they once understood\nThe bell in the tower has lost its sharp tongue\nWhile the oldest of anthems are waiting be sung\nThe copper is tarnishing on the fountain of youth\nAs we trade in our secrets for a version of truth\n\n[Verse]\nThe windows are frosted with a layer of time\nSearching for a reason in a ladder to climb\nThe merchants of worry are closing their stalls\nWhile the writing is fading on the crumbling walls\nIt\u2019s a cold hard rain on a tin plated roof\nSearching for a sign or a shadow of proof\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe shadows are stretching like fingers of fate\nTracing the lines on an iron gate\nThe silence is louder than the thunder could be\nAnd the wind is a river flowing out to the sea\n\n[Chorus]\nPlay it again for the hearts in the dark\nLeaving behind every smoldering spark\nTurning the corner where the pavemen