  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe needle slides across the heavy black groove\nStatic crackles like a dry summer storm\nWe watched the previous spin fade into the dust\nWhile the shadows grew long against the cabin wall\nThe stories told are buried in the sleeve\nWaiting for a needle to find the vein of truth\n\n[Chorus]\nNow give us the next song to carry the weight\nOf a morning that hasn't found its color yet\nTurn the page of the rolling mercury sea\nAnd play the one that knows where we are headed\nBeyond the broken fences of the tired world\n\n[Verse]\nGrandfather left his boots by the iron stove\nHis lungs filled with the ghosts of coal and pride\nHe never stayed for the final flickering note\nHe was always looking toward the rising ridge\nWhere the wind whistles a tune no man can own\nJust a restless hum beneath the frozen ground\n\n[Chorus]\nNow give us the next song to carry the weight\nOf a morning that hasn't found its color yet\nTurn the page of the rolling mercury sea\nAnd play the one that knows where we are headed\nBeyond the broken fences of the tired world\n\n[Bridge]\nIt is not about the melody we already memorized\nOr the rhymes that fell like spent silver coins\nIt is the silence that follows the closing chord\nThe hunger for a sound that hasn't been named\nCalling out from the throat of a brand new day\n\n[Chorus]\nNow give us the next song to carry the weight\nOf a morning that hasn't found its color yet\nTurn the page of the rolling mercury sea\nAnd play the one that knows where we are headed\nBeyond the broken fences of the tired world\n\n[Chorus]\nGive us the next song for the highway ahead\nWhere the asphalt bleeds into the golden horizon\nLet the chords strike like a hammer on the anvil\nAnd sing the verse that sets the prisoner free\nUntil the music is all that remains of the journey",
