  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe blank page is white as a winter gale\nA steady hand starts to carve out the trail\nWhere the ink meets the fibers of a silent mind\nLeaving all the hollow ghost stories behind\nI picked up the dust from a sun-beaten road\nTo lighten the weight of a heavy old load\n\n[Verse]\nThere is a crack in the window where the breeze comes through\nBringing a scent of the morning and the heavy dew\nI watched the horizon pull away from the shore\nNot searching for answers or locking the door\nJust putting one foot where the other has been\nWitnessing the cycle of the world begin\n\n[Chorus]\nFirst song rising from a quiet throat\nSending out a message on a wooden boat\nNo map for the water no stars in the sky\nJust the honest truth and a reason why\nThe first song is the hardest one to sing\nWaiting for the copper bell to finally ring\n\n[Bridge]\nThey told me the path was already defined\nBy the kings and the paupers who left us behind\nBut I broke the compass and I burned the chart\nTo find the raw pulse of a wandering heart\nIt is not about the glory or the silver prize\nIt is about the clarity in a stranger\u2019s eyes\n\n[Verse]\nThe shadows are long but the fire is bright\nCutting a hole through the belly of the night\nEvery word is a pebble thrown into the deep\nWaking the memories that used to sleep\nNow the ink is dry and the air is clear\nThere is nothing left to hold or to fear\n\n[Chorus]\nFirst song rising from a quiet throat\nSending out a message on a wooden boat\nNo map for the water no stars in the sky\nJust the honest truth and a reason why\nThe first song is the hardest one to sing\nWaiting for the copper bell to finally ring",
