  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nI scratched a line upon the slate to see if it would hold\nThe ink is pale and the morning air is bitter and cold\nLooking for a spark in the ashes of a burnt out fire\nWalking the wire between the truth and the liar\nThe wheels are turning but the road remains the same\nTrying once more to remember a forgotten name\n\n[Chorus]\nOh it is the test of the spirit and the test of the mind\nLeaving the shadows and the hollow years behind\nStarting the engine in the middle of a dream\nNothing is ever quite as simple as it would seem\nAgain and again until the hammer hits the nail\nSetting the compass for a different kind of sail\n\n[Bridge]\nThe clock on the wall has nothing new to tell\nJust the ringing of a distant and heavy iron bell\nStacked up failures like stones in a garden wall\nWaiting for the sky or the curtain to finally fall\n\n[Verse]\nThe pages are blank and the pen is heavy in my hand\nSearching for a foothold in the shifting desert sand\nIf the first notes stumbled then the next ones might fly\nUnder the heavy weight of a bruised and purple sky\nNo use in hiding what the silence has to say\nWhen the sun is breaking through the curtains of the day\n\n[Chorus]\nOh it is the test of the spirit and the test of the mind\nLeaving the shadows and the hollow years behind\nStarting the engine in the middle of a dream\nNothing is ever quite as simple as it would seem\nAgain and again until the hammer hits the nail\nSetting the compass for a different kind of sail",
