  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe morning ink is drying on a page of unlined white\nA traveler is tracing silhouettes against the light\nThe inkwell holds the heavy dust of roads already known\nA sparrow perches on the fence to reap what has been sown\nWe measure out our progress by the shadows on the wall\nWaiting for the hammer or the final bugle call\n\n[Chorus]\nThe compass needle flickers in the palm of every hand\nWriting out a message in the shifting desert sand\nIt is another cycle of the spinning wooden wheel\nSearching for a substance that the senses cannot feel\nThe blueprint is a ghost that haunts the architecture plan\nThe mystery remains inside the spirit of a man\n\n[Chorus]\nThe compass needle flickers in the palm of every hand\nWriting out a message in the shifting desert sand\nIt is another cycle of the spinning wooden wheel\nSearching for a substance that the senses cannot feel\nThe blueprint is a ghost that haunts the architecture plan\nThe mystery remains inside the spirit of a man\n\n[Verse]\nA merchant sells a map that leads to nowhere in the rain\nThe conductor counts the boxcars on a rusted ghost of train\nYou say that every trial is a lesson for the soul\nBut the broken pieces never make a decorated whole\nThe dictionary fails to find a name for how we stand\nGazing at the borders of a strange and hollow land\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe clock is ticking backwards in the hallway of the mind\nLeaving all the certainty and heavy boots behind\nThe mirror shows a stranger with a familiar kind of gaze\nWalking through the thicket of the autumn colored haze\n\n[Chorus]\nThe compass needle flickers in the palm of every hand\nWriting out a message in the shifting desert sand\nIt is another cycle of the spinning wooden wheel\nSearching for a substance that the senses cannot feel\nThe blueprint is a ghost that haunts the architecture plan\nThe mystery remains inside the spirit of a man\n\n[Chorus]\nThe compass needle flickers in the palm of every hand\nWriting out a