  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe white paper sits like a desert in the sun\nWaiting for the first drop of rain to fall from a pen\nYou say it is only a trial a simple run\nBut every heavy heart knows exactly where to begin\nThe dust on the shelf is a witness to the crime\nOf the minutes we wasted just waiting for a sign\n\n[Chorus]\nThis is the moment where the wire meets the spark\nTesting the gravity and the shadows in the dark\nBeyond the perimeter where the quiet secrets lie\nUnder the vastness of a pale and restless sky\nEverything is real until the fever fades away\nJust a small experiment in the middle of the day\n\n[Verse]\nI saw the ghosts of the poets stacking stones\nBuilding a monument out of old forgotten names\nThey left their marrow and their weary restless bones\nTo stay out of the reach of the hungry blowing flames\nYou try the handle just to see if it will turn\nWhile the ancient lessons are the ones you never learn\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe measure of the distance is a jagged broken line\nSearching for a vintage in a dying patch of vine\nA knock upon the window or a hollow crystal sound\nLooking for a treasure that was never meant for ground\n\n[Chorus]\nThis is the moment where the wire meets the spark\nTesting the gravity and the shadows in the dark\nBeyond the perimeter where the quiet secrets lie\nUnder the vastness of a pale and restless sky\nEverything is real until the fever fades away\nJust a small experiment in the middle of the day",
