  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe needle drops on a different groove today\nTracing the lines that the first one threw away\nIt is the shadow cast by the morning sun\nA slower walk before the frantic run\nDust settles on the polished black veneer\nWhile the static hums a melody only I can hear\nNo more rehearsals for a play that ended wrong\nJust the steady pulse of the second song\n\n[Chorus]\nIt is the rewrite of the jagged page\nThe quieter step on a wider stage\nNot the scream but the breath held tight\nThe silver glow of the middle night\nComing after the thunder and the rain\nTo wash the salt from the open vein\nSteady and deep and staying long\nListen to the ghost of the second song\n\n[Bridge]\nThe first was a wildfire burning out of breath\nChasing a ghost and flirting with its death\nBut this one moves like the tide against the pier\nPatient and cold and crystal clear\nIt does not care if the crowd forgets to stay\nIt has its own debt and its own price to pay\n\n[Verse]\nI found the chords in a box beneath the bed\nBetween the things I did and those I said\nThey do not crash like the waves against the shore\nThey just knock softly at the heavy door\nNo desperate reach for the highest flying note\nJust the honest words stuck inside the throat\nThe fever broke and the world is moving on\nTo the measured beat of the second song\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe applause has faded to a distant gray\nThe golden idols have been packed away\nNow the air is thin and the light is pale\nBut the ship is set for a longer sail\n\n[Chorus]\nIt is the rewrite of the jagged page\nThe quieter step on a wider stage\nNot the scream but the breath held tight\nThe silver glow of the middle night\nComing after the thunder and the rain\nTo wash the salt from the open vein\nSteady and deep and staying long\nListen to the ghost of the second song",
