  "lyrics": "[Verse]\nThe first time I spoke was a question to the sky\nThe second was a heavy truth that passed the locals by\nNow the dust settles on the windowsill of the day\nAnd I have found a different way to say what I must say\nThe shadows stretch across the floorboards in the hall\nTracing lines of every season since the leaves began to fall\nI am picking up the pieces of a melody once lost\nCounting out the silver coins to pay the final cost\n\n[Chorus]\nThis is the third song rising from the hollow of the wood\nA testament to standing where the older giants stood\nBeyond the simple greeting and the parting of the veil\nA steady hand across the sea to guide the tattered sail\nNo more the frantic searching for a name to call my own\nJust the low vibrations of a seed that has been sown\nThe air is clear and quiet as the sun begins to fade\nIn the circle of the music that the honest men have made\n\n[Bridge]\nThree times the bell went ringing through the valley and the town\nThree times the heavy burden had to lay its leather down\nI am not the boy who started when the morning mist was high\nI am just a witness to the turning of the eye\nThe narrative is shifting like the current in the stream\nWaking from the fever of a long and restless dream\n\n[Verse]\nTake this verse and fold it like a letter in your palm\nA small and sturdy anchor in a momentary calm\nI have spent the early hours chasing ghosts along the wall\nBut the third song is the one that learns to weather through it all\nThe ink is drying slowly on the parchment of the night\nEverything I hid away is stepping to the light\nThe repetition fades into a singular refrain\nLike a dry and thirsty meadow drinking up the sudden rain\n\n[Chorus]\nThis is the third song rising from the hollow of the wood\nA testament to standing where the older giants stood\nBeyond the simple greeting and the parting of the veil\nA steady hand across the sea to guide the tattered sail\nNo more the frantic searching for a name to call my own\nJust the low vibrations of a seed that has been sown\nThe air is clear and quiet as the sun begins to fade\nIn the circle of the music that the honest men have made",
